// Ambition's motion techniques (schema `motion_techniques`, owned by the
// projectile capability): the gestures the player fire system asks for by
// id. A technique fires when any one of its patterns is in the recent input,
// in order (other directions may come between). `invert_facing` fires the
// direction opposite the one the gesture ends on. The compiler refuses a
// technique with no patterns and an empty pattern: no input fires either.
// An edit here is played at the next start, or after a content
// reload, with no Rust build.
//
// `qcf_grace` (`Down, Right`) is a part of `qcf` (`Down, DownRight, Right`),
// so the fire system asks for `qcf` and `hcf` first: the file states the
// patterns, and the fire system owns which one wins.
{
    // Quarter-circle forward, and its mirror.
    "qcf": (patterns: [[Down, DownRight, Right], [Down, DownLeft, Left]]),
    // The quarter-circle without its diagonal: the keyboard-friendly road to
    // the weaker Hadouken.
    "qcf_grace": (patterns: [[Down, Right], [Down, Left]]),
    // Half-circle, and its mirror. It fires against the facing it ends on.
    "hcf": (
        patterns: [[Right, DownRight, Down, DownLeft, Left], [Left, DownLeft, Down, DownRight, Right]],
        invert_facing: true,
    ),
}
